  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rehabilitation of  Angola IDPs Basic School</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is for the rehabilitation of Angola IDPs basic school in Omdurman, Khartoum state.  The school which is originally constructed in local materials and was destroyed by 2009 floods, if a centre for 650 children all of whom are the children of people displaced by the civil war in the South, East and West of the country.  These are some of more Economically and socially marginalised areas in Sudan; they lack access to basic services such as education. The project which will provide education to 650 children in Angol, will be be implemented by the Catholic Archdiocese of Khartoum, Education secretariat with support from CAFOD and it will be coordinated with Ministry of Education and Guidance in Khartoum State as well as Education department of Omdurman/Angola localities.</narrative>
  </description>
